            <ArticleTitle>[The intra-arterial use of lidocaine to reduce pain in aorto-femoral arteriography (author's transl)].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1001-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In 50 patients subjected to aorto-femoral arteriography, the examination was carried out with and without the addition of 1 cm3 of 2% lidocaine per 10 cm3 of contrast medium; in 43/50 lidocaine led to a more or less notable reduction in pain without side-effects.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
